In article <251@telenet.telenet.com> news@telenet.telenet.com (News) writes:
	[some gripes on surviving and chances of finding certain objects]
	   How do you survive when you put on a pair of cursed boots of
	   levitation when you've never found a scroll of remove curse
	   and your god is angry with you because you have on a helm of
	   reverse alignment?
* SPOILER ALERT *

Sinks have finally found some special use, in addition to the fountain-like
use and the fairly silly use of determining ring types...
Just try floating over one !

	   I'm not saying that the game should be a gimme, but we have
	   experienced players here who have never gotten below level 10.
	   The only thing I can think of is that there is either something
	   wrong with the logic, or something wrong with the percentage
	   chance of things, or something wrong with the way random
	   numbers are generated.

Yes, I can agree with this.  After reading rec.games.hack and messing around
with Hack for ages, I still haven't made it very far in NH3.  Most of the time,
the game just gets more or less boring since nothing very interesting is found
and you die of normal run-of-the-mill-level-3-and-below monsters.

By the way, should zoos, throne rooms and the three stooges work as up to now ?
Or have they become lower-level stuff ?  Since I've played NH3 quite a lot and
haven't yet bumped into any of the three... yes, we should have all options
set.
